Primacy with a digestive system similar to the human, with the plant resources available in the savannah, it is difficult to meet the needs for amino acids.
In addition, if this need cannot be satisfied, there are serious consequences: lag in growth, malnutrition and, ultimately, death.
Easily accessible plant sources would be proteins present in leaves and legumes, which are hardly digestible for primates, which also include us, if they are not cooked.
Conversely, animal food (ants, termites, eggs) is not only easily digestible, but also a source of high-quality proteins that contains all the essential amino acids.
